{
	"$comment": [
		"Labelled cases for the harness pillars, read by the TypeScript benchmark (bench.ts) and meant to be read by any other implementation of the harness.",
		"Each label is what a careful developer would want, not what the code happens to do.",
		"A case with `open` reproduces a known defect that `open` names. Open cases are reported, kept out of the floors, and must still reproduce: a fix that makes one pass also removes its `open` field.",
		"`knownGaps` and `knownFalsePrompts` are accepted limits of a text classifier, not defects to fix."
	],
